      {
        "id": 123449,
        "name": "Mezike",
        "username": "Mezike",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c6cbf5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-17T14:41:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"grysqrl\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/48/1909_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> grysqrl:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Last time I tried pestering someone for 3 years, I recieved a retraining order. Now I am counting the days until I can see Emma Stone again.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWhat did you get trained in (evidently not so well the first time)?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This was back in the days when he failed his 1st Grade Acolyte Certificate of Excellence, his inability to fully unlock the dire powers of the dimensions beyond our own resulted in class detention, five lashes with a Birch stick, and three years of additional Incantation Class after school. That was where he evidently met Emma Stone and eventually received the retraining order from her, which gave him the extra attention that he needed to pass the crucial end of term exam with flying colours. So enamoured was our cursed friend with his new qualification that he is clearly champing at the bit to once again see the person who made it all possible for him in the hopes of achieving further academic excellence under her tutelage.</p>",
