      {
        "id": 123450,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-17T15:02:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"UXM266\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/48/1966_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> UXM266:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I have not found anything saying that Lillian Merle Corvus is becoming a hero. It seems that Christopher, that magnificent bastard that he is, has not confirmed 100% that she is becoming a hero. it justs eems that he's playing with all of our specualtion and guessing. Unless I missed something, can somone help a friend out?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There is a bunch of interlocking clues and hints that point to this happening, but it hasnt been confirmed anywhere. I think I've outlined most of them in various threads long since dead. But the single biggest piece of evidence for this is found in Parse's deck. The art shows Progeny grabbing Matriarch in a not-so-playful way, and Capt Cosmic rushing to, presumably, save her.</p>\n<p>The thing is, there is no art ever released in the history of SotM that shows villain vs villain action. Could it? Sure. But it's been a long time and never happened, so theres a reason adam choose to draw the scene the way he did (besides the fact that its a shout-out to a Fantastic 4 comic cover). That could have been anybody Cap was trying to save. Why Matty?</p>\n<p>The way I see it, Matriarch gets saved from the clutches of an evil that spells out the end of the world which becomes the tipping point for her transformation to hero status. That and I stand by my original Matriarch speculation that ties her to the big-bad from my footesnotes post on her.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:57:20.955Z",
